    "result_text": "The full test suite passes. Only `AcceptanceTest` is a runnable test class (the other two test files are the base class and a helper), and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `capacityWarning` following the existing `bulkSignupWarning` pattern:\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added `isCityApproachingCapacity(city)` (true when the city already holds 40\u201349 owners) plus a shared `cityOwnerCount(city)` helper that `isCityAtCapacity` now also uses. The warning is set in `assignDerivedAttributes` via `owner.setCapacityWarning(...)`. The hard rejection at 50 in `checkForConflicts`/`isCityAtCapacity` is unchanged.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `capacityWarning` field (`@Column(name = \"capacity_warning\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `capacityWarning` boolean to the owner schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it by name automatically.\n\n4. **Schema files** (h2, hsqldb, postgres, mysql) \u2014 Added the `capacity_warning` column so the value persists and is read back on `GET`.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` (fill a fresh city to 40, next owner warns) passes, and the build is green.",
